From 91e4d0b329dab287baf80e09d87e607a668d6332 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <Github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 11:11:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Register the /com/palm/power category only once

SuspendInit() calls com_palm_suspend_lunabus_init() directly - it needs
the categories in place before it spawns the suspend thread - but the
function was also still registered as an INIT_FUNC at the same
INIT_FUNC_END priority. Whichever ran second failed its first
LSRegisterCategory with "Category /com/palm/power already registered"
and then never reached the /suspend registration on the
com.webos.service.power handle, logging two LUNASERVICE ERROR lines on
every single start of the daemon. Drop the INIT_FUNC registration and
keep the explicit, ordered call.
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/pwrevents/suspend_ipc.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/pwrevents/suspend_ipc.c b/src/pwrevents/suspend_ipc.c
index f54cc6c..d10ad1a 100644
--- a/src/pwrevents/suspend_ipc.c
+++ b/src/pwrevents/suspend_ipc.c
@@ -893,6 +893,10 @@ error:
     return -1;
 }
 
-INIT_FUNC(INIT_FUNC_END, com_palm_suspend_lunabus_init);
+/* com_palm_suspend_lunabus_init() is called from SuspendInit(), which needs
+ * the categories in place before it spawns the suspend thread. It must not
+ * also be registered as an INIT_FUNC: both ran at INIT_FUNC_END, so the
+ * second invocation tried to register /com/palm/power again and failed with
+ * "Category /com/palm/power already registered" on every start. */
 
 /* @} END OF SuspendIPC */
